  "rule": "Two ways to say how you feel, and English uses \"I'm\" for both.\n\nWith a describing word (an adjective), use *estar*:\n*estoy cansado*, *estoy enfermo*, *estoy nervioso*, *estoy ocupado*, *estoy bien*\n\nWith a noun, the feeling is something you have, so use *tener*:\n*tengo sed*, *tengo hambre*, *tengo frío*, *tengo sueño*, *tengo miedo*\n\nThe test: could you put \"a lot of\" in front of it in English? A lot of thirst works, so *tener*. A lot of ill doesn't, so *estar*.\n\nAnd remember: describing words change for a woman (*enferma*, *contenta*), but *sed* never changes.",
  "smallPrint": "*Estar* + adjective vs *tener* + noun for physical and emotional states.",
